.\" saphira-llm(1) - native GGUF inference for BitNet b1.58
.TH SAPHIRA-LLM 1 "2026" "saphira-llm 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
saphira\-llm \- native C11 GGUF inference runtime for BitNet b1.58 (CPU, x86-64-v3)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira\-llm
.B \-m
.I MODEL
.B \-p
.I PROMPT
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira\-llm
loads a GGUF model, encodes a prompt, generates a continuation greedily and
writes the decoded text to standard output.
.PP
The runtime is self-contained: the container reader, the tensor layer, the
vector kernels, the thread pool and the CPU ISA dispatch are all in this
binary. There is no Python, no BLAS, and no launcher around another engine.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " MODEL" "\fR, \fP" \-\-model= MODEL
Path to a GGUF model. Required for anything beyond container inspection.
.TP
.BI \-p " PROMPT" "\fR, \fP" \-\-prompt= PROMPT
Prompt text to condition on.
.TP
.BI \-n " N" "\fR, \fP" \-\-n\-predict= N
Tokens to generate. Default 64.
.TP
.BI \-c " N" "\fR, \fP" \-\-ctx= N
Context size in tokens. Default 4096.
.TP
.BI \-t " N" "\fR, \fP" \-\-threads= N
Worker threads. 0 is not accepted; pass a value.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-place
Do not pin threads to a placement plan, for measuring the placement contrast.
.TP
.BI \-\-isa " LEVEL"
Force an ISA floor:
.BR v3 ", " vnni ", " avx512 ", " amx " or " auto .
Requesting a level this CPU does not have is a hard error, never a silent
downgrade.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " LEVEL"
.BR quiet ", " error ", " warn ", " info " (default) " or " debug .
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version and the compiled ISA baseline.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage.
.SH LIMITS
One prompt per invocation. There is no interactive mode and no chat template,
so a question is treated as text to continue rather than as an instruction to
follow; a base model given a question will often repeat it.
.PP
Generation is greedy: argmax at every step. There is no temperature, top\-p,
top\-k or repetition penalty, and no seed. Greedy output is deterministic, so
the same prompt and model always give the same tokens.
.PP
The 2B BitNet b1.58 2B\-4T GGUF is not packaged. Supply your own via
.BR \-m .
.SH MODELS
Only architecture
.B bitnet\-b1.58
is implemented. A GGUF of any other architecture is refused with
.I unsupported\-architecture
rather than loaded and mis-executed. Weights may be I2_S ternary, F32, F16,
BF16, Q8_0 or Q4_0; the K\-quants are recognised and refused by name.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MODEL
Default model path used by
.BR saphira\-llm-testsuite .
.TP
.B THREADS
Default thread count for
.BR saphira\-llm-testsuite .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira\-llm\-tgbench (1),
.BR saphira\-llm\-kernelbench (1),
.BR saphira\-llm\-testsuite (1)
